  "title": "The Lost Star in the Dance",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "perception and hidden objects",
  "premise": "A choreographer must find a star badge among five moving dancers, but rapid position swaps make guessing unreliable. They pause the formation at each beat and track the badge-bearing dancer by a distinct square shoe, then reveal that the star was always pinned on that dancer’s back.",
  "hook": "Follow the shoe, not the sparkle.",
  "visible_action": "Five figures swap marked positions; square shoe remains consistent; freeze frames show the path; final dancer turns to expose the badge.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Use a stable identifier when positions keep changing.",
  "gate": "Maintain identity and badge continuity in every frame; present as this specific tracking puzzle, not a test of intelligence or attention.",
